From phase0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: Phase 0 - LRZ_VSC_CONTROL=0x03 post-clear

After 19 falsifications of the A22X period-8 cycle, deeper analysis of
the closed-source webOS libGLESv2.so decompilation revealed the
proprietary stack writes A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL=0x03 during the
binning pass setup in leia_configure_binning_pass @ 0x00134a50.

Mesa upstream writes 0x00 ("disabled") here. Phase 0 experiment:
change to 0x03 and observe. If cycle collapses we win without full
hw-binning port. If null, full port required.

Reference: reports/a22x-hw-binning-port-analysis.md

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c	2026-05-11 15:09:10.715425078 +0200
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c	2026-05-11 15:09:43.352350677 +0200
@@ -342,9 +342,10 @@
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_RB_COPY_CONTROL));
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
 
+   /* Phase 0: LRZ_VSC_CONTROL=0x03 matching webOS binning-pass value */
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_A220_RB_LRZ_VSC_CONTROL));
-   OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
+   OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000003);
 
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_VGT_VERTEX_REUSE_BLOCK_CNTL));
